.TH SVC 8 "2026-11-09" "nni @VERSION@" "nni family manual"
.SH NAME
svc \- the nni service manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B svc
.RB [ list ]
.br
.B svc
.BR start | stop | restart | status
.I NAME ...
.br
.B svc
.BR enable | disable
.I NAME ...
.br
.B svc log
.I NAME
.RB [ \-f ]
.br
.B svc new
.I NAME COMMAND
.br
.B svc edit
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
YnniOS and SGnniOS have no systemd: busybox is the init program.
.B svc
starts long\-running programs (services, also called daemons), keeps each
one under a small supervisor that starts it again if it dies, and saves
everything the program prints in
.IR /var/log/nni/NAME.log .
It works the same on both distributions.
.PP
A service whose program dies five times in a row within five seconds of
starting is given up on and shown as
.B FAILED
by
.BR "svc list" ;
fix the cause, then start it again.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Every service, whether it starts at boot, and whether it is running.
.TP
.BI start " NAME"
Start now. Does not change what happens at boot.
.TP
.BI stop " NAME"
Stop now (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after five seconds).
.TP
.BI restart " NAME"
Stop, then start.
.TP
.BI status " NAME"
State, process ID, boot setting, command and log file of one service.
.TP
.BI enable " NAME"
Start at every boot, and start it now.
.TP
.BI disable " NAME"
Do not start at boot, and stop it now.
.TP
.BI log " NAME " \fR[\fB\-f\fR]
The last 40 lines of the service's log;
.B \-f
keeps following new lines.
.TP
.BI new " NAME COMMAND"
Create a service file from a command line.
.TP
.BI edit " NAME"
Open the service file in
.B $EDITOR
(vi by default).
.TP
.BR boot ", " shutdown
Used by the boot script and by
.I /etc/inittab
to start the enabled services and to stop everything on poweroff.
.SH SERVICE FILES
Each service is described by
.IR /etc/nni/services/NAME.svc ,
a small file of shell variables:
.TP
.B DESC
One line saying what it is.
.TP
.B CMD
The command. It must stay in the foreground: do not use options such as
\-d or \-\-daemon that send the program to the background, because
.B svc
does that itself.
.TP
.B PRE
Optional command run before every start, for example to create a directory.
.TP
.B USER
Optional user to run the command as.
.TP
.B RESTART
.B no
for a job that should run once and not be restarted.
.PP
Example,
.IR /etc/nni/services/web.svc :
.PP
.nf
DESC="my web server"
PRE="mkdir \-p /srv/www"
CMD="httpd \-f \-p 8080 \-h /srv/www"
.fi
.PP
Ready\-made services: syslogd, klogd, crond, ntpd, acpid, httpd, sshd and
dbus.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/nni/services/
Service files.
.TP
.I /etc/nni/enabled/
One empty file per service that starts at boot.
.TP
.I /run/nni/svc/
Process IDs of running services.
.TP
.I /var/log/nni/
Service logs (rotated at 1 MB).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
svc list
svc enable ntpd
svc new myapp "/usr/local/bin/myapp \-\-foreground"
svc log myapp \-f
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nni (8),
.BR handbook (1)
